  "description": "EZEZOA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C132 H200 Gd12 N6 O68 2-,5(C1 H4 O1),3(Na1 1+),H1 O1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd10 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd11 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd12 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.805-3.977 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.52-112.49°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C137H213Gd12N6Na3O74. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
